---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "[DD Month YYYY, set this when you publish]";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="What cookies and local storage Fellowshell uses, and how to control them."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated-note text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </header>

      <p>
        This page explains what cookies and browser storage this site uses,
        why, and how you can change your choice at any time. It should be
        read alongside our{" "}
        <a class="link" href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How consent works here</h2>
      <p>
        When you first visit, a banner asks you to accept or reject
        non-essential storage. Nothing beyond what's strictly necessary is
        set before you choose. You can change your mind at any time using
        the <strong>"Cookie preferences"</strong> link in the site footer,
        which reopens the same choice.
      </p>

      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>fellowshell:consent</code></td>
            <td>Local storage, strictly necessary</td>
            <td>Remembers your cookie choice so we don't ask on every visit</td>
            <td>Until cleared or reset</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>fellowshell_consent</code></td>
            <td>First-party cookie, strictly necessary</td>
            <td>Mirrors your cookie choice</td>
            <td>12 months</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Analytics storage</td>
            <td>Optional, only if accepted</td>
            <td>
              Aggregate usage measurement (pages viewed, approximate
              location, device type) to help us improve the site. No
              analytics script runs until you opt in.
            </td>
            <td>[Set once an analytics tool is chosen]</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        We currently set no third-party or advertising cookies. If that
        changes, for example by adding an analytics provider, this table
        and the consent banner categories will be updated first.
      </p>

      <h2>Controlling cookies in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        Alongside the controls on this site, most browsers let you block or
        delete cookies in their settings. Blocking strictly necessary
        storage may mean the cookie banner reappears on every visit, since we
        can no longer remember your earlier choice.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email{" "}
        <a class="link" href="mailto:privacy@fellowshell.com">privacy@fellowshell.com</a>{" "}
        with any questions about this policy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
